{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1348, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nA string S is given.\nFind how many places in S have A, B, and C in this order at even intervals.\nSpecifically, find the number of triples of integers (i,j,k) that satisfy all of the following conditions. Here, |S| denotes the length of S, and S_x denotes the x-th character of S.\n\n- 1 \\leq i < j < k \\leq |S|\n- j - i = k - j\n- S_i = A\n- S_j = B\n- S_k = C\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nS\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- S is an uppercase English string with length between 3 and 100, inclusive.\n\nSample Input 1\n\nAABCC\n\nSample Output 1\n\n2\r\n\nThere are two triples (i,j,k) = (1,3,5) and (2,3,4) that satisfy the conditions.\n\nSample Input 2\n\nARC\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0\n\nSample Input 3\n\nAABAAABBAEDCCCD\n\nSample Output 3\n\n4\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1382, "char_start": 1360, "quote": "Input:\nAABCC\nOutput:\n2", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1414, "char_start": 1394, "quote": "Input:\nARC\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1458, "char_start": 1426, "quote": "Input:\nAABAAABBAEDCCCD\nOutput:\n4", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "8babaff11194f227cd014124c173a01016e776fdccbdb02427f62f0b052d2411", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "258d036de79af1161376e3410e53270b9f7e4abc97b7cd8a12e781767b268047", "seq": 2}
